            <ArticleTitle>No sustainability without health equity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S24-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.puhe.2012.05.018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article suggests that opportunities to make strategic linkages between health, well-being and sustainable development are missed too often. There is a need for a more sophisticated understanding of the current landscape, which builds on the links between sustainable development, health, well-being and social justice. There is a need for a more sophisticated understanding of health economics to inform policy decisions, ensuring that the impact of mega-externalities (e.g. obesity) are considered and inform planning and policy decisions.</AbstractText>
